{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-psalms-106",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 106,
  "title": "Psalms 106",
  "display_title": "Psalms 106",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "psalms",
  "book": "Psalms",
  "bookName": "Psalms",
  "bookOrder": 19,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 106,
  "sortOrder": 19106,
  "verseCount": 48,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Praise ye the LORD. O give thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Who can utter the mighty acts of the LORD? who can shew forth all his praise?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Blessed are they that keep judgment, and he that doeth righteousness at all times.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Remember me, O LORD, with the favour that thou bearest unto thy people: O visit me with thy salvation;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "That I may see the good of thy chosen, that I may rejoice in the gladness of thy nation, that I may glory with thine inheritance.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "We have sinned with our fathers, we have committed iniquity, we have done wickedly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Our fathers understood not thy wonders in Egypt; they remembered not the multitude of thy mercies; but provoked him at the sea, even at the Red sea.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Nevertheless he saved them for his name’s sake, that he might make his mighty power to be known.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "He rebuked the Red sea also, and it was dried up: so he led them through the depths, as through the wilderness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "And he saved them from the hand of him that hated them, and redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "And the waters covered their enemies: there was not one of them left.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Then believed they his words; they sang his praise.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "They soon forgat his works; they waited not for his counsel:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "But lusted exceedingly in the wilderness, and tempted God in the desert.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And he gave them their request; but sent leanness into their soul.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "They envied Moses also in the camp, and Aaron the saint of the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan, and covered the company of Abiram.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And a fire was kindled in their company; the flame burned up the wicked.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "They made a calf in Horeb, and worshipped the molten image.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Thus they changed their glory into the similitude of an ox that eateth grass.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "They forgat God their saviour, which had done great things in Egypt;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Wondrous works in the land of Ham, and terrible things by the Red sea.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Therefore he said that he would destroy them, had not Moses his chosen stood before him in the breach, to turn away his wrath, lest he should destroy them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Yea, they despised the pleasant land, they believed not his word:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "But murmured in their tents, and hearkened not unto the voice of the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "Therefore he lifted up his hand against them, to overthrow them in the wilderness:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "To overthrow their seed also among the nations, and to scatter them in the lands.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "They joined themselves also unto Baalpeor, and ate the sacrifices of the dead.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Thus they provoked him to anger with their inventions: and the plague brake in upon them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Then stood up Phinehas, and executed judgment: and so the plague was stayed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "And that was counted unto him for righteousness unto all generations for evermore.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "They angered him also at the waters of strife, so that it went ill with Moses for their sakes:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "Because they provoked his spirit, so that he spake unadvisedly with his lips.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "They did not destroy the nations, concerning whom the LORD commanded them:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "But were mingled among the heathen, and learned their works.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "And they served their idols: which were a snare unto them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:36"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-037",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 37,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:37",
      "numberLabel": "37",
      "text": "Yea, they sacrificed their sons and their daughters unto devils,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:37",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:37"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-038",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 38,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:38",
      "numberLabel": "38",
      "text": "And shed innocent blood, even the blood of their sons and of their daughters, whom they sacrificed unto the idols of Canaan: and the land was polluted with blood.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:38",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:38"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-039",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 39,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:39",
      "numberLabel": "39",
      "text": "Thus were they defiled with their own works, and went a whoring with their own inventions.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:39",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-040",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 40,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:40",
      "numberLabel": "40",
      "text": "Therefore was the wrath of the LORD kindled against his people, insomuch that he abhorred his own inheritance.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:40",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:40"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-041",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 41,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:41",
      "numberLabel": "41",
      "text": "And he gave them into the hand of the heathen; and they that hated them ruled over them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:41",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-042",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 42,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:42",
      "numberLabel": "42",
      "text": "Their enemies also oppressed them, and they were brought into subjection under their hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:42",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:42"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-043",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 43,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:43",
      "numberLabel": "43",
      "text": "Many times did he deliver them; but they provoked him with their counsel, and were brought low for their iniquity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:43",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:43"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-044",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 44,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:44",
      "numberLabel": "44",
      "text": "Nevertheless he regarded their affliction, when he heard their cry:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:44",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:44"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-045",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 45,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:45",
      "numberLabel": "45",
      "text": "And he remembered for them his covenant, and repented according to the multitude of his mercies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:45",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:45"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-046",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 46,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:46",
      "numberLabel": "46",
      "text": "He made them also to be pitied of all those that carried them captives.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:46",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:46"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-047",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 47,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:47",
      "numberLabel": "47",
      "text": "Save us, O LORD our God, and gather us from among the heathen, to give thanks unto thy holy name, and to triumph in thy praise.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:47",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:47"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-048",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 48,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:106:48",
      "numberLabel": "48",
      "text": "Blessed be the LORD God of Israel from everlasting to everlasting: and let all the people say, Amen. Praise ye the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 106:48",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:106:48"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
